{"comparisons":[],"failures":[],"frontier":[],"initial":{"controlled-language":{"coverage":[{"reason":"States the compulsory route and revised transition date.","status":"INTERPRETED","unit_id":"u1"},{"reason":"Background heading.","status":"CONTEXT","unit_id":"u2"},{"reason":"Identifies e-IP, WINGS, launch history and an earlier circular whose contents are not supplied.","status":"CONTEXT","unit_id":"u3"},{"reason":"Establishes acceptance of existing channels during the original parallel run; read with the extension.","status":"INTERPRETED","unit_id":"u4"},{"reason":"Heading connecting the extension and enhancements.","status":"CONTEXT","unit_id":"u5"},{"reason":"Describes monitoring and feedback, without imposing a submission duty.","status":"CONTEXT","unit_id":"u6"},{"reason":"Extends the parallel run through 29 November 2024 and explains its purpose.","status":"INTERPRETED","unit_id":"u7"},{"reason":"Full-adoption heading supports the transition context.","status":"CONTEXT","unit_id":"u8"},{"reason":"Restates the mandatory route, identifies integrated reporting and distinguishes optional fee settlement.","status":"INTERPRETED","unit_id":"u9"},{"reason":"Enquiries heading.","status":"CONTEXT","unit_id":"u10"},{"reason":"Review commitment and contact guidance; practicability qualifies enhancement, not the compulsory route.","status":"INTERPRETED","unit_id":"u11"},{"reason":"Identifies the issuing division.","status":"CONTEXT","unit_id":"u12"},{"reason":"Identifies the issuing regulator.","status":"CONTEXT","unit_id":"u13"},{"reason":"End marker.","status":"CONTEXT","unit_id":"u14"},{"reason":"Product enumeration supports competing closed-list and descriptive-list scope readings.","status":"INTERPRETED","unit_id":"u17"},{"reason":"Expands WINGS; does not establish an additional submission route.","status":"CONTEXT","unit_id":"u18"}],"dimensions":[{"dimension":"scope","explanation":"The control concerns persons making applications or submissions for IPD-administered investment products, without specifying a particular regulated actor class. Whether the footnote closes the product universe is uncertain.","source_unit_ids":["u1","u9","u17"],"status":"AMBIGUOUS"},{"dimension":"definitions","explanation":"e-IP is the online application/submission system, IPD is the Investment Products Division, and WINGS expands to Web-based INteGrated Service. The product footnote supplies categories but no express exhaustive or illustrative label.","source_unit_ids":["u1","u3","u17","u18"],"status":"AMBIGUOUS"},{"dimension":"exceptions","explanation":"Existing channels remain accepted during the extended parallel run. No post-transition exception is stated. The phrase 'where practicable' attaches to SFC review and enhancement, not submission duties.","source_unit_ids":["u4","u7","u9","u11"],"status":"PROPOSED"},{"dimension":"modality","explanation":"'Must' makes the submission route compulsory; 'can also' makes annual-fee settlement an optional facility. Integration and enhancement announcements do not independently create reporting or payment duties.","source_unit_ids":["u7","u9","u11"],"status":"PROPOSED"},{"dimension":"time","explanation":"The original 29 October 2024 endpoint is extended to 29 November 2024; compulsory e-IP submission begins on 30 November 2024. The 8 July circular and 29 July launch are historical dates. Treatment of later documents in already-open cases is not expressly addressed.","source_unit_ids":["u1","u3","u4","u7","u9"],"status":"PROPOSED"},{"dimension":"dependencies","explanation":"The earlier launch circular and existing IPD submission requests may clarify classification and mechanics, but their contents and the packet's external-authorities dependency are unavailable. No enhancement-completion condition attaches to the stated transition date.","source_unit_ids":["u3","u7","u9"],"status":"AMBIGUOUS"}],"questions":["Does footnote 1 exhaustively delimit covered products, or describe the products currently administered by IPD?","For an application begun before 30 November 2024, must every subsequent submission use e-IP, and what event determines the submission date?","Do the earlier launch circular or existing IPD requests specify migration procedures, route exceptions or product classifications absent from this packet?"],"readings":[{"assumptions":["The assessed item is a particular application or submission, not an assessment of institutional compliance.","Footnote 1 exhaustively identifies the covered product categories.","Extending the parallel run preserves existing-channel acceptance through 29 November 2024.","The date fact concerns the assessed submission event; the packet does not resolve dispatch versus receipt."],"citations":[{"quote":"applications and submissions of investment products administered by the Investment Products Division (IPD)1 must be submitted to IPD via e-IP from 30 November 2024.","unit_id":"u1"},{"quote":"1 Investment-linked assurance schemes, mandatory provident fund products, open-ended fund companies, paper gold schemes, pooled retirement funds, real estate investment trusts, unit trusts and mutual funds and unlisted structured investment products.","unit_id":"u17"},{"quote":"During this period, the SFC continues to accept applications and submissions via existing channels.","unit_id":"u4"},{"quote":"the SFC will extend the parallel run period of e-IP by one month to 29 November 2024.","unit_id":"u7"},{"quote":"In addition, e-IP users can also settle recurring annual fees associated with relevant investment products through the new system.","unit_id":"u9"}],"distinction":"Closed-list reading: an IPD-administered product outside every enumerated category falls outside this selected control. The strongest uncertainty is that the footnote never expressly says its enumeration is exhaustive.","family":"scope","formalization":{"facts":[{"meaning":"The assessed item is an application or submission concerning an investment product administered by IPD; fee settlement alone does not qualify.","name":"ipd_product_submission","requires_judgment":true,"source_unit_ids":["u1","u3","u9"],"type":"bool","unit":"Boolean"},{"meaning":"The investment product concerned falls within at least one category enumerated in footnote 1.","name":"listed_product_category","requires_judgment":true,"source_unit_ids":["u17"],"type":"bool","unit":"Boolean"},{"meaning":"Gregorian date of the assessed submission event, with the operative event determined before supplying this fact.","name":"submission_date","requires_judgment":true,"source_unit_ids":["u1","u9"],"type":"date","unit":"Gregorian calendar date"},{"meaning":"The assessed application or submission is submitted to IPD via e-IP.","name":"submitted_via_eip","requires_judgment":false,"source_unit_ids":["u1","u9"],"type":"bool","unit":"Boolean"}],"result":"submitted_via_eip","result_type":"bool","scope":"(and ipd_product_submission listed_product_category (>= submission_date (date 2024-11-30)))"},"local_id":"r1","questions":["Is the unqualified product enumeration intended as an exhaustive scope definition?"],"statement":"Selected control—compulsory e-IP route: from 30 November 2024, a person submitting an application or submission concerning an IPD-administered product within footnote 1's categories must use e-IP. Existing channels remain available during the extended parallel run. Optional annual-fee settlement is outside this route requirement.","subject":"Compulsory e-IP submission route with a closed product list"},{"assumptions":["The assessed item is a particular application or submission, not an assessment of institutional compliance.","IPD administration determines product coverage; footnote 1 describes that coverage without restricting the operative general wording.","Extending the parallel run preserves existing-channel acceptance through 29 November 2024.","The date fact concerns the assessed submission event; the packet does not resolve dispatch versus receipt."],"citations":[{"quote":"Starting 30 November 2024, ie, after the parallel run period, applications and submissions of investment products administered by IPD must be submitted via e-IP.","unit_id":"u9"},{"quote":"1 Investment-linked assurance schemes, mandatory provident fund products, open-ended fund companies, paper gold schemes, pooled retirement funds, real estate investment trusts, unit trusts and mutual funds and unlisted structured investment products.","unit_id":"u17"},{"quote":"The current submission requests from IPD via the IP E-submission system will be integrated into e-IP, including reporting of net asset values, large redemptions and suspensions of dealing.","unit_id":"u9"},{"quote":"The SFC will continue to review and enhance the operation of e-IP where practicable.","unit_id":"u11"}],"distinction":"Administration-based reading: a product outside the listed categories is nevertheless covered if IPD administers it. This relies on the operative general wording, especially its repetition in u9. Its strongest weakness is that footnote 1 contains no illustrative marker such as 'including'; the competing readings matter only if an IPD-administered product falls outside the enumeration.","family":"scope","formalization":{"facts":[{"meaning":"The assessed item is an application or submission concerning an investment product administered by IPD; fee settlement alone does not qualify.","name":"ipd_product_submission","requires_judgment":true,"source_unit_ids":["u1","u3","u9"],"type":"bool","unit":"Boolean"},{"meaning":"The investment product concerned falls within at least one category enumerated in footnote 1.","name":"listed_product_category","requires_judgment":true,"source_unit_ids":["u17"],"type":"bool","unit":"Boolean"},{"meaning":"Gregorian date of the assessed submission event, with the operative event determined before supplying this fact.","name":"submission_date","requires_judgment":true,"source_unit_ids":["u1","u9"],"type":"date","unit":"Gregorian calendar date"},{"meaning":"The assessed application or submission is submitted to IPD via e-IP.","name":"submitted_via_eip","requires_judgment":false,"source_unit_ids":["u1","u9"],"type":"bool","unit":"Boolean"}],"result":"submitted_via_eip","result_type":"bool","scope":"(and ipd_product_submission (>= submission_date (date 2024-11-30)))"},"local_id":"r2","questions":["Can an investment product be administered by IPD while falling outside every footnote 1 category?"],"statement":"Selected control—compulsory e-IP route: from 30 November 2024, a person making any application or submission concerning an IPD-administered investment product must use e-IP. The listed reporting integrations explain the route's operation without independently imposing reporting duties. The transition is not conditional on completion of enhancements, and fee settlement remains optional.","subject":"Compulsory e-IP submission route determined by IPD administration"}]},"normative":{"coverage":[{"reason":"Establishes the selected mandatory route, product scope and transition date.","status":"INTERPRETED","unit_id":"u1"},{"reason":"Background heading; creates no separate requirement.","status":"CONTEXT","unit_id":"u2"},{"reason":"Identifies launch history, WINGS and application/submission functions; referenced launch circular is not supplied.","status":"CONTEXT","unit_id":"u3"},{"reason":"Establishes acceptance of existing channels during the parallel run, read with its extension.","status":"INTERPRETED","unit_id":"u4"},{"reason":"Section heading connecting extension and enhancements.","status":"CONTEXT","unit_id":"u5"},{"reason":"Describes monitoring and feedback, without a submission duty.","status":"CONTEXT","unit_id":"u6"},{"reason":"Extends the parallel run through 29 November 2024; enhancements explain the extension.","status":"INTERPRETED","unit_id":"u7"},{"reason":"Full-adoption heading supports the transition context.","status":"CONTEXT","unit_id":"u8"},{"reason":"Restates the mandatory route, identifies integrated reporting and distinguishes optional annual-fee payment.","status":"INTERPRETED","unit_id":"u9"},{"reason":"Enquiries heading; creates no submission requirement.","status":"CONTEXT","unit_id":"u10"},{"reason":"Practicability qualifies SFC operational enhancements; contact guidance does not qualify the mandatory route.","status":"INTERPRETED","unit_id":"u11"},{"reason":"Division attribution.","status":"CONTEXT","unit_id":"u12"},{"reason":"Commission attribution.","status":"CONTEXT","unit_id":"u13"},{"reason":"End marker.","status":"CONTEXT","unit_id":"u14"},{"reason":"Product list supports competing exhaustive and descriptive readings of scope.","status":"INTERPRETED","unit_id":"u17"},{"reason":"Expands WINGS; supplies no additional routing obligation.","status":"CONTEXT","unit_id":"u18"}],"dimensions":[{"dimension":"scope","explanation":"The control concerns persons making applications or submissions to IPD for investment products it administers, rather than every activity of an institution. Whether footnote 1 exhaustively limits product coverage remains uncertain.","source_unit_ids":["u1","u9","u17"],"status":"AMBIGUOUS"},{"dimension":"definitions","explanation":"e-IP is the online application/submission system; IPD is the Investment Products Division; WINGS is expanded in footnote 2. Footnote 1 lists products without expressly saying whether the list is exhaustive.","source_unit_ids":["u1","u3","u17","u18"],"status":"AMBIGUOUS"},{"dimension":"exceptions","explanation":"Existing channels remain available during the extended parallel run. No post-transition exemption is stated. 'where practicable' attaches to SFC review and enhancement, not submission through e-IP.","source_unit_ids":["u4","u7","u9","u11"],"status":"PROPOSED"},{"dimension":"modality","explanation":"'must' imposes the selected routing requirement; integration and enhancements are announced system changes. 'can also' describes an optional annual-fee facility and does not require its use or establish a new fee duty.","source_unit_ids":["u1","u7","u9","u11"],"status":"PROPOSED"},{"dimension":"time","explanation":"The launch was 29 July 2024; the original parallel-run endpoint of 29 October is extended to 29 November. Compulsory routing starts on 30 November 2024. Treatment of later communications in already-pending cases is not expressly addressed.","source_unit_ids":["u1","u3","u4","u7","u9"],"status":"PROPOSED"},{"dimension":"dependencies","explanation":"The 8 July launch circular and dependency external-authorities.24ec50 are not supplied. Their contents cannot establish further definitions, migration rules or exemptions here. The stated transition date is not expressly conditional on completion of enhancements or integration.","source_unit_ids":["u3","u7","u9"],"status":"AMBIGUOUS"}],"questions":["Is footnote 1 an exhaustive definition of covered investment products or a descriptive list of IPD's current remit?","Does the referenced 8 July 2024 circular specify how communications in cases opened before 30 November 2024 must migrate?","What operative material is represented by external-authorities.24ec50, and does it supply relevant scope or transition qualifications?"],"readings":[{"assumptions":["Footnote 1 limits the product scope of the immediately preceding mandatory-routing provision.","The relevant date is the date of the individual application or submission, including a later submission in an existing case.","The extension preserves acceptance of existing channels through 29 November 2024.","The formalization tests only the named routing control for an individual submission; it does not establish an underlying duty to submit or whole-institution compliance."],"citations":[{"quote":"After the extended period, applications and submissions of investment products administered by the Investment Products Division (IPD)1 must be submitted to IPD via e-IP from 30 November 2024.","unit_id":"u1"},{"quote":"1 Investment-linked assurance schemes, mandatory provident fund products, open-ended fund companies, paper gold schemes, pooled retirement funds, real estate investment trusts, unit trusts and mutual funds and unlisted structured investment products.","unit_id":"u17"},{"quote":"During this period, the SFC continues to accept applications and submissions via existing channels.","unit_id":"u4"},{"quote":"To facilitate these enhancements, the SFC will extend the parallel run period of e-IP by one month to 29 November 2024.","unit_id":"u7"},{"quote":"In addition, e-IP users can also settle recurring annual fees associated with relevant investment products through the new system.","unit_id":"u9"},{"quote":"The SFC will continue to review and enhance the operation of e-IP where practicable.","unit_id":"u11"}],"distinction":"Under this narrower reading, a submission concerning an IPD-administered product outside every listed category falls outside the selected control. The strongest uncertainty is that the footnote never expressly states that its list is exhaustive.","family":"scope","formalization":{"facts":[{"meaning":"The assessed event is an investment-product application or submission to IPD, rather than only use of the annual-fee payment facility.","name":"is_application_or_submission","requires_judgment":true,"source_unit_ids":["u1","u3","u9"],"type":"bool","unit":"Boolean"},{"meaning":"IPD administers the investment product concerned in the assessed event.","name":"product_administered_by_ipd","requires_judgment":true,"source_unit_ids":["u1","u9"],"type":"bool","unit":"Boolean"},{"meaning":"The investment product concerned belongs to at least one category listed in footnote 1.","name":"product_in_footnote_list","requires_judgment":true,"source_unit_ids":["u17"],"type":"bool","unit":"Boolean"},{"meaning":"The Gregorian calendar date on which the assessed application or submission is made.","name":"submission_date","requires_judgment":false,"source_unit_ids":["u1","u9"],"type":"date","unit":"Gregorian calendar date"},{"meaning":"The assessed application or submission is submitted to IPD through e-IP.","name":"submitted_via_eip","requires_judgment":false,"source_unit_ids":["u1","u9"],"type":"bool","unit":"Boolean"}],"result":"submitted_via_eip","result_type":"bool","scope":"(and is_application_or_submission product_administered_by_ipd product_in_footnote_list (>= submission_date (date 2024-11-30)))"},"local_id":"r1","questions":["Does the footnote have a limiting definitional function?","How should hybrid products or disputed category membership be classified?"],"statement":"Selected control—compulsory e-IP routing: an application or submission to IPD made on or after 30 November 2024 must use e-IP when it concerns an IPD-administered product within footnote 1's enumerated categories. The extended parallel run permits existing channels through 29 November. Optional fee payment and practicability of SFC enhancements do not qualify this routing duty.","subject":"Compulsory e-IP routing with an exhaustive product list"},{"assumptions":["The operative phrase 'investment products administered by IPD' determines product coverage; footnote 1 describes that remit without closing it.","The relevant date is the date of the individual application or submission, including a later submission in an existing case.","The extension preserves acceptance of existing channels through 29 November 2024.","The formalization tests only the named routing control for an individual submission; it does not establish an underlying duty to submit or whole-institution compliance."],"citations":[{"quote":"Starting 30 November 2024, ie, after the parallel run period, applications and submissions of investment products administered by IPD must be submitted via e-IP.","unit_id":"u9"},{"quote":"The current submission requests from IPD via the IP E-submission system will be integrated into e-IP, including reporting of net asset values, large redemptions and suspensions of dealing.","unit_id":"u9"},{"quote":"1 Investment-linked assurance schemes, mandatory provident fund products, open-ended fund companies, paper gold schemes, pooled retirement funds, real estate investment trusts, unit trusts and mutual funds and unlisted structured investment products.","unit_id":"u17"},{"quote":"During this period, the SFC continues to accept applications and submissions via existing channels.","unit_id":"u4"},{"quote":"To facilitate these enhancements, the SFC will extend the parallel run period of e-IP by one month to 29 November 2024.","unit_id":"u7"},{"quote":"In addition, e-IP users can also settle recurring annual fees associated with relevant investment products through the new system.","unit_id":"u9"}],"distinction":"This reading also reaches any IPD-administered investment product outside the listed categories. It draws support from u9's unqualified restatement of the IPD-administered scope. Its strongest uncertainty is that footnote 1's direct attachment in u1 may make that list limiting. No unlisted product is presumed to exist.","family":"scope","formalization":{"facts":[{"meaning":"The assessed event is an investment-product application or submission to IPD, rather than only use of the annual-fee payment facility.","name":"is_application_or_submission","requires_judgment":true,"source_unit_ids":["u1","u3","u9"],"type":"bool","unit":"Boolean"},{"meaning":"IPD administers the investment product concerned in the assessed event.","name":"product_administered_by_ipd","requires_judgment":true,"source_unit_ids":["u1","u9"],"type":"bool","unit":"Boolean"},{"meaning":"The investment product concerned belongs to at least one category listed in footnote 1.","name":"product_in_footnote_list","requires_judgment":true,"source_unit_ids":["u17"],"type":"bool","unit":"Boolean"},{"meaning":"The Gregorian calendar date on which the assessed application or submission is made.","name":"submission_date","requires_judgment":false,"source_unit_ids":["u1","u9"],"type":"date","unit":"Gregorian calendar date"},{"meaning":"The assessed application or submission is submitted to IPD through e-IP.","name":"submitted_via_eip","requires_judgment":false,"source_unit_ids":["u1","u9"],"type":"bool","unit":"Boolean"}],"result":"submitted_via_eip","result_type":"bool","scope":"(and is_application_or_submission product_administered_by_ipd (>= submission_date (date 2024-11-30)))"},"local_id":"r2","questions":["Can the descriptive function of footnote 1 be confirmed from the referenced material?","Which submissions fall within IPD administration, including migrated reporting requests?"],"statement":"Selected control—compulsory e-IP routing: all applications and submissions to IPD concerning investment products it administers must use e-IP from 30 November 2024, with footnote 1 describing rather than exhaustively restricting the covered products. The extended parallel run ends on 29 November. Integration includes the identified reporting requests, while annual-fee payment remains an optional facility.","subject":"Compulsory e-IP routing determined by IPD administration"}]}},"java_checks":[],"live_provider":true,"model_calls":2,"no_progress":0,"nodes":[],"pending":null,"provider_id":"codex.fresh.v1","retrievals":[],"rounds":0,"roundtrips":[],"run_id":"run.53099b8c078642398be286ed2cd842de","stop":null}